    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nInterested in this property? Sign up for mySherryFitz to arrange your viewing, see current offers or make your own offer. Register now at SherryFitz.ie.\n\nSherry FitzGerald Conor McManus are delighted to present Fintully, Clontibret, Co. Monaghan to the market.\n\nThis most appealing detached property has been meticulously cared for and maintained, offering a wonderful opportunity to acquire a comfortable family home in a pleasant rural setting. \n\nThe pristine accommodation briefly comprises, an entrance hall, sitting room, dining room, kitchen, four bedrooms, bathroom, separate WC and hot press. \n\nBeautifully maintained gardens surround the residence, with mature hedging providing excellent privacy and shelter. To the rear is a patio area ideal for outdoor dining, complemented by colourful planted borders and neatly maintained lawns. \n\nFintully is a home that reflects considerable care and attention over the years and is sure to appeal to purchasers seeking a well-maintained detached bungalow with generous outdoor space, all within easy reach of Monaghan Town.\n\nViewing is highly recommended."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall: - \nBright and welcoming entrance hall featuring attractive wood flooring and neutral décor. The glazed entrance door and side panels allow plenty of natural light.\n\nSitting Room: - \nAn elegantly presented reception room featuring a striking marble fireplace with gas fire, decorative coving and ceiling rose. A large picture window overlooks the beautifully maintained front garden, while wood-effect flooring completes the room.\n\nLiving/ Dining Room: - \nA beautifully presented dual-aspect room offering defined areas for both dining and relaxed everyday living. Features include an attractive fireplace, decorative coving and ceiling rose, wood flooring and generous windows overlooking the mature gardens.\n\nKitchen: - \nA fresh and inviting kitchen, fitted with an excellent range of cream shaker-style wall and floor units, complimented by contrasting worktops and integrated appliances, including a double oven. A large window provides plenty of natural light and pleasant garden views, while wood flooring flows seamlessly through the space.\n\nGuest WC: - \nConveniently located guest WC comprising wash hand basin and WC, finished in neutral tones with wood-effect flooring.\n\nBedroom 1: - \nA bright and well-proportioned double bedroom featuring extensive built-in wardrobes and dressing area, wooden floor covering and a large window enjoying pleasant countryside views.\n\nBedroom 2: - \nA bright and inviting double bedroom with built-in wardrobes providing excellent storage and wooden floor covering.\n\nBedroom 3: - \nA well-presented double bedroom with built-in wardrobes, wooden floor covering and a large window overlooking the mature gardens.\n\nBedroom 4: - \nA well-presented single bedroom with wooden floor covering and a large window overlooking the mature gardens.\n\nBathroom: - \nStylish and contemporary bathroom, fully tiled in a neutral finish and comprising a freestanding roll-top bath, separate corner shower enclosure, wash hand basin with vanity unit and WC.\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li>Total floor area: 116 sq mts ( 1249 sq ft) approximately</li><li>Surrounding lands: 0.61 HA (1.50 acres) approximately</li><li>Situated on a spacious mature site with beautifully maintained gardens and established landscaping</li><li>Basement for additional storage</li><li>Pleasant countryside views and an attractive rural setting</li><li>Generous private parking and extensive hard-surfaced areas surrounding the residence</li><li>Convenient access onto the DublinDerry Road (N2), ideal for commuters</li><li>Approximately 10 minutes' drive from Monaghan Town</li><li>Convenient to Clontibret village and surrounding amenities</li><li>Oil-fired central heating </li><li>Broadband available</li><li>Double glazing</ul>"
      },
